1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:08,509
June nineteen sixty-two. High above Alcatraz's cellblock, three inmates engineered an escape out of raincoats.

2
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:15,957
Over months, they stole more than fifty rubberized coats, cutting and stitching them into a six by fourteen foot hull.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,738
To seal the seams watertight, they clamped the rubber against hot prison steam pipes, vulcanizing the joints.

4
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:31,878
For inflation, they converted a musical concertina into a hand-pumped bellows, driving air through a single red valve.

5
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,982
On the night of June eleventh, with hand-carved wooden paddles, they pushed off into San Francisco Bay.

6
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:43,675
The raft held. By morning, only the tide remained.
